; A program that needs a **third** walk, which is why the answer is a fixpoint
; and not a fixed number of passes.
;
; Two forward `br`s. The second one shrinks in the second walk, which pulls
; `far` one byte closer -- and only then does the first one come into range.
;
;   walk 1   everything forward is assumed long
;              br far at 0 (3), 123 nops, br mid at 126 (3), mid 129, far 130
;   walk 2   using walk 1's table
;              br far: 130 - 2 = 128, one out of reach, stays long
;              br mid: 129 - 128 = 1, fits, shrinks to two bytes
;              far is now 129, and the program is 130 bytes
;   walk 3   using walk 2's table
;              br far: 129 - 2 = 127, fits. Both short, and the program is 129
;   walk 4   nothing moves, so the driver stops
;
; So the second walk is not a fix, it is one round of one. Every round makes
; the next round's estimate better, and the only stopping rule that is right
; for every program is **until nothing moves**, which is what the driver says.
; Until 2026-09-23 this file was in `divergent/`, at 130: the description
; stopped after walk 2.
;
; `chain.z80` is the same shape one round shallower, and `three-rounds.z80`
; one round deeper.
        br far
